f:["$","$L17",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-the-existing-options-traded-away","title":"What the existing options traded away"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-three-properties","title":"The three properties that drove the design"},{"depth":2,"url":"#licensing","title":"Licensing, precisely"},{"depth":2,"url":"#versioning","title":"Versioning"},{"depth":2,"url":"#why-these-docs-were-rewritten","title":"Why these docs were rewritten"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"full":"$undefined","children":[["$","$L18",null,{"children":"History and licensing"}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":"What Forge was built to replace, the three properties that drove the rewrite, and exactly how the source is licensed."}],["$","$L1a",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone evaluating Forge against an existing build\nfarm, and anyone who needs to answer a licensing question precisely. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What\nyou'll have at the end:"}]," the design pressures that produced the current\nsystem, and a file-by-file account of what license applies. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," ten\nminutes."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Remote build execution is not a new idea. Google shipped an internal version\nof it long before the\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/remote-apis","children":"Remote Execution API"}]," was\npublished, and by the early 2020s there were several open implementations of\nthe published protocol. Forge started in December 2020 as a Rust\nimplementation of the CAS half of that protocol (first called Rust CAS, then\nTurbo Cache from April 2022), was renamed to Forge in December 2023\n(the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cas"}]," executable became ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge"}]," at the same time), and cut its\nfirst tagged release, 0.1.0, on 2023-12-20. The\nargument for writing a new implementation rather than running an existing\none is the one below: the protocol is narrow enough that a rewrite is\ntractable, and what was expensive in the existing options was the substrate."]}],"\n",["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-the-existing-options-traded-away","children":"What the existing options traded away"}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"className":"relative overflow-auto prose-no-margin my-6","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Family"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Strength"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"The recurring problem"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"JVM-based servers"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Mature, complete, well understood"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Tail latency under GC pressure, and a memory footprint that makes horizontal scaling the only answer"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Go services"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Fast on the happy path, straightforward to operate"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Contention on hot artifacts and on control-plane locks, which shows up as a cluster-wide stall rather than a slow request"}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Proprietary clouds"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Fast, someone else operates it"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"No source access, and pricing that scales with the thing you are trying to do more of"}]]}]]}]]}]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Two of those three problems are runtime problems rather than design problems.\nThat observation is the whole argument for the rewrite: the protocol was\nfine, the storage model was fine, and what was expensive was the substrate."}],"\n",["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-three-properties","children":"The three properties that drove the design"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Predictable latency."}]," In a build system, the p99 is the number developers\nexperience: a single stalled action blocks everything downstream of it in\nthe graph. Removing the garbage collector removes a class of latency spike\nthat is very hard to tune away rather than eliminate."]}],"\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35"]}],"$L36"]}]
